GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT


Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In late summer, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated 
a campaign of conquest in Kaluga, a Plain province owing allegiance to Circe 
(#8).  Migfox (#65)'s armies took possession of Kaluga practically 
uncontested.
  In spring, Tlazolteotl (#88) rode her flying armies over to Big Sky.
  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
marched on the Mountain province of Big Sky, a land garrisoned by the 
soldiers of Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88) was in command of the invading 
armies.  The defending forces were led by Alexius (#12).  Tlazolteotl (#88)
's campaign accomplished the conquest of Big Sky.
  In early summer, Tlazolteotl rode her flying armies into Moongard.
  A host of warriors carried the banner of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0) into the Mountain province of Moongard, ruled by Circe (#8).  
Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces took Moongard without any major battles.
  In spring, Alain (#33) rode his flying armies over to Khalturin.
  An army coming from the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded Khalturin, hoping to conquer that province owned by Circe (#8) and 
made up of extensive Plains.  Khalturin was conquered and occupied by Alain 
(#33)'s host.
  In fall, Alain rode his flying armies into Katmai.
  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Forest province of Katmai, 
ruled by Agesilao (#9).  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Katmai without any 
major battles.


Kingdom of Prometeo (#5):
  In fall, an army coming from the empire of Prometeo (#5) entered Shasta, 
hoping to subjugate that province ruled by the provincial Eagle chieftain 
and made up of extensive Mountains.  Prometeo was in command of the invading 
armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
Though Prometeo's host were triumphant, the provincial Eagle chieftain 
regrouped its men and decided to contest Shasta.
  In fall, Tarsus (#43) rode his flying armies into Waterford.  Waterford 
was conquered and occupied by Tarsus's fleet.
  In early summer, Marlon (#68) rode into Abu Matariq.  Marlon was told by 
some sheepherders of a perilous feature in Abu Matariq previously unknown to 
us, an Ancient Megaliths where dwells the Renegade Necromancer.
  In late summer, Marlon moved into Kiska.
  In early winter, Marlon journeyed to Abu Matariq.
  In spring, Shasta was hit by a plague.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In early summer, Hume (#77) moved into Orielle.
  In fall, Hume rode into Macondo.  Hume was informed by some sheepherders 
of a perilous feature in Macondo, a Monastery inhabited by the Genie.


Kingdom of Circe (#8):
  In spring, an army coming from the empire of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded Khalturin, hoping to conquer 
that province owned by Circe (#8) and made up of extensive Plains.  
Khalturin was conquered and occupied by Alain (#33)'s host.

  In early summer, a host of warriors carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Mountain province of Moongard,
ruled by Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces took Moongard without any 
major battles.

  In late summer, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated 
a campaign of conquest in Kaluga, a Plain province owing allegiance to Circe 
(#8).  Migfox (#65)'s armies took possession of Kaluga practically 
uncontested.

  In spring, soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)
ian empire marched on the Mountain province of Big Sky, a land garrisoned by 
the soldiers of Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88) was in command of the 
invading armies.  The defending forces were led by Alexius (#12).  
Tlazolteotl (#88)'s campaign accomplished the conquest of Big Sky.
  In fall, Jolin (#37) journeyed to Transylvania.
  In early winter, Jolin travelled to Abu Matariq.


Kingdom of Agesilao (#9):
  In fall, a host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Forest province of Katmai, 
ruled by Agesilao (#9).  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Katmai without any 
major battles.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in Tactics.  At levels 5 and 
up, the automatic 20% per level increase in army strength is discontinued.  
Instead, your characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  TACTICAL WARGAME MASTERY:  The chance for a unit to increase in quality 
when Practicing Tactics (or Naval) is increased by 100% (example: an Average 
unit now has a 10% chance to improve per phase).


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached level 6 in Tactics.  Your characters of 
this high level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  TACTICAL MASTERY:  The armies commanded by a character at a battle are 
increased in strength by 15%.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained level 5 in Marches.  At levels 5 and 
up, the "Ability Level 4" on the March Table is used, and the usual 
increases in army speed on land are not necessarily continued.  Instead, 
your characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  MARCH THROUGH FLOODS:  By using pontoon bridges, ferries and so forth, it 
becomes possible for armies to enter or leave any province affected by the 
Flood spell.  One movement point is deducted from all units which have to 
use this ability, after they have moved.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 6 in Marches.  All 
characters of this exalted level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  MARCH CAVALRY:  The character adds one to the movement rate of land armies 
which start with 3 or more movement points.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 5 in Meleeing.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 10% per level increase in the chance to hit in 
melee is discontinued, as well as the damage plus (however, skill level will 
still determine who attacks first in combat).  Instead, all characters of 
this exalted level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  MELEE- EVASION:  A character becomes expert at evading opponents when 
using the Flee tactic.  Slow opponents can always be evaded, Medium-speed 
opponents can be evaded 20% of the time, and Fast opponents are evaded 50% 
of the time.


END MOVES REPORT

